-- title:
--   Restriction of the transported local fundamental class generates H²(S,K_w^×)
-- statement:
--   Let $E \subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$ Galois, let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $D =$ [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) be the decomposition subgroup of $K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} K$ attached to the valuation subring of the $w$-adic valuation, assumed solvable as a group. Let $q$ be a prime and $L$ a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, carrying an action of $D$ by semiring automorphisms and a compatible action on $L^\times$, and let $\Phi\colon K_w \to L$ be a ring isomorphism from the $w$-adic completion. It is assumed that $D$ fixes all $\mathbb{Q}_q$-scalars of $L$, that the action on $L^\times$ is induced by that on $L$, and that $\Phi$ is $D$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a further finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ with $K_0 \le L$ and $\{x \in L : x \in K_0\}$ exactly the $D$-fixed elements of $L$. Let $\theta$ be a morphism of $\mathbb{Z}$-linear $D$-representations from the additive form of $L^\times$ to that of $K_w^\times$ which on underlying groups is $y \mapsto \Phi^{-1}(y)$, and let $u \in H^2(D, L^\times)$ satisfy the predicate [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass q L D K₀`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60), i.e. for every unramified overlayer datum $(M,H,N_L,N_n,e,\varphi,\pi)$ over $(L,D,K_0)$ and every compatible comparison map $\iota$, the pullback of $u$ along $e^{-1}\circ(\,\cdot\,\bmod N_L)$ equals the inflation of the class of the explicit carry $2$-cocycle built from the Frobenius lift $\varphi$ and the uniformiser $\pi$. Then, for every subgroup $S \le D$, writing $c$ for the restriction to $S$ of the image $\theta_*(u) \in H^2(D, K_w^\times)$: every class $z \in H^2(S, K_w^\times)$ equals $m \cdot c$ for some $m \in \mathbb{Z}$, and $m \cdot c = 0$ if and only if $\#S$ divides $m$.
--
--   This is the statement, in the form used downstream, that for each subgroup of a decomposition group the local cohomology group $H^2(S, K_w^\times)$ is cyclic of order $\#S$, generated by the restriction of the local fundamental class transported from $L^\times$ to $K_w^\times$ along the chosen isomorphism of the completion with a $q$-adic field. It supports the reading of the individual terms of a double-coset decomposition of a corestricted class as integers measured against one fundamental class per place, and is the subgroup companion of the statement for $S = D$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_PlaceDecomp_exists_eq_zsmul_map_subtype_and_zsmul_eq_zero_iff_of_isLocalFundamentalClass.lean

